# REGRESSION -- Track B3 (D31-uniform, indirect call sigil gate): the PARAM cell
# of the callable-shape axis. When the callee is a `Callable[void(&int)]`
# PARAMETER (not a local), a bare argument at the invocation site must REJECT
# at `gg check` with `E_OwnershipMismatch` -- exactly as the LOCAL cell does
# (`indirect_call_bare_arg_amp_callee_error.gg`).
#
# AXIS / CELL:
#   Callable PARAM callee  x  bare arg vs `&`-declared param
# The PARAM shape used to hide behind an ownership check that skipped
# non-DefId callees; Option A's type-based indirect path fires uniformly.
#
# Pre-B3 (RED-verified at HEAD 1028972f): `gg check` printed "OK: no semantic
# errors"; the emitted binary silently dropped the intended mutation (the
# indirect PARAM call fell through the sidecar-transplant path that only
# fires when the caller explicitly writes `&`).
# Post-B3: `gg check` REJECTS with `E_OwnershipMismatch` at the argument span.
void invoke(Callable[void(&int)] cb, int a):
    # THE ASSERTION: bare `cb(a)` REJECTS -- the callable param declares `&`;
    # the caller must re-spell `cb(&a)`.
    cb(a)

void bump(int &n):
    n = n + 100

void main():
    int a = 1
    invoke(bump, a)
    print(a)
